# Backend architecture

Stack: **Bun + Elysia + TypeScript, Drizzle + PostgreSQL** (source: `golive-gate/data/build-contract.json` `allowedStack`). Reference: `code-structure/data/backend-layout.json`.

Legacy projects (Vibe Start before 2026-10-07) keep their existing backend (e.g. Node/Express); audit against their existing structure as advisory, do not convert.

## Directory layout (`apps/backend/src/`)

| Directory | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `index.ts` | One fluent Elysia chain; `export type App = typeof app` |
| `modules/` | Feature modules (Elysia plugins) |
| `config/` | App configuration |
| `plugins/` | Cross-cutting Elysia plugins (auth, errors, CORS) |
| `database/` | Drizzle client, `schema/`, `migrations/` |
| `utils/` | Backend-only utilities |
| `types/` | Backend-only types |

## Module pattern (`modules/<feature>/`)

```
routes.ts       # Elysia chained plugin: HTTP + TypeBox validation only
model.ts        # TypeBox schemas (single validator)
service.ts      # Business logic
repository.ts   # Drizzle queries
types.ts        # Module-local types
```

## Requirements

- Routes: `new Elysia({ prefix }).get(...).post(...)` — parse, validate with TypeBox, call service, return — **no business logic, no DB queries**
- Services: all business rules and orchestration
- Repositories: all Drizzle queries (parameterized; no string-concatenated SQL)
- Build the app as **one fluent chain** and export `typeof app` — separate `app.get(...)` statements discard route types and Eden treaty collapses to `{}`
- Conditional routes and static fallbacks go inside a handler, not outside the chain
- Unions: `t.Union([t.Literal('a'), t.Literal('b')])`, never mapped from a constant
- Cross-cutting concerns are Elysia plugins composed with `.use()`, not Express-style middleware
- Shared types with frontend → `packages/shared-types`

## Config & secrets placement

- All secrets/config are read **once, at the boundary** — a `config/` module that reads
  `process.env` (populated from a managed secrets store) and **validates required values at
  startup, failing fast** on missing/malformed/placeholder secrets. Feature code imports typed
  config from `config/`, never `process.env` directly and never hard-coded literals.
- Cryptographic-key handling (KEK/DEK envelope, blind-index keys) stays isolated in `utils/`
  behind a small wrap/unwrap interface, so the rest of the code is agnostic to where the key lives
  (see `code-review` → `apply-security-patterns`).

## On violation

Refactor: move queries to repository, logic to service, HTTP handling to the routes plugin.
